 {"id":"AUG-059-R2","title":"[P1] RECURRENCE of AUG-059: `answer --domain` silently skips the coverage advance for the 35 of 44 domains whose grid row carries `terminating_ring: null` — `status` then keeps printing 'answered ... (row status NOT-REACHED)'","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"status":"complete","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T21:00:00Z","created_by":null,"capability_tags":["domain-coverage","status","substrate-write"],"reasoning":"AUG-059 (closed, complete) was 'status contradicts itself on one line: a domain is reported answered while the same line says (row status NOT-REACHED)'; its fix was `advance_domain_status` (auger.py:3949), called from `answer` (auger.py:5648) to retire the seed word when an answer lands in a domain. The contradiction is BACK in real use, and the cause is not the display: the advance WRITE is rejected by the substrate for most of the grid.\nARM PAIR, same verb, same project, same substrate, minutes apart (`-p P-20261027152017`, namespace df18 on a scratch DuckBrain :3918, HEAD a9c979bcd2ab6a92a5ef4f513b5b030e0a67169a):\n  a) `answer --id D-001 ... --domain 4.05` -> 'D-001 recorded (domain 4.05 = data, ...)' PLUS '  domain     4.05 -> REACHED (seed status retired)'; the substrate's own row reads status=REACHED (GET /api/ns/df18/tables/domain?num=eq.4.05).\n  b) `answer --id D-002 ... --domain 4.03` -> the same success line and NO advance line; the row stays status=NOT-REACHED. Repeated for 4.09 (no advance) and 4.06 (advanced) — the split follows the domain, not the run.\n  c) `status` then prints the AUG-059 line verbatim: '  4.03  identity  answered  triage 2  floor 2  ...  decisions/questions 1  (row status NOT-REACHED)'.\nROOT CAUSE, proven with raw substrate calls on the same rows: PATCH /api/ns/df18/tables/domain?pk=eq.DM-000003 with {\"status\":\"REACHED\"} answers 422 {\"error\":\"Column 'terminating_ring' (integer) requires an integer number, got null in table 'domain'\",\"code\":\"UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY\"}. Arms: the SAME body against the integer-ring row DM-000005 answers 200 {\"updated\":1}; {\"owner\":\"probe\"} on DM-000003 answers the same 422 (so it is not the status field); sending \"terminating_ring\": null explicitly in the body answers the same 422 (so a caller cannot patch it away). auger declares the column integer (auger.py:236, COLS['domain']) while the grid files themselves say `terminating_ring: null — domain was not opened` for 35 of the 44 domains (census via GET domain?limit=300: 88 rows, 35 null in the first 44-row slice; list in the report), and the substrate's INSERT path accepted those nulls — so the store holds 35 rows its own update path can never modify.\nThe skip is by design ('Every failure here is SKIPPED — never fatal', auger.py:3981-3987 returns \"\" and `answer` prints nothing) and that is right for the answer, but it means the failure is INVISIBLE: the user is told the seed status was retired only when it was, and never told when it was not. The usage skill currently documents the resulting line as a display quirk ('trust the leading word, not the parenthetical') — see AUG-113 — which is why this survived 30+ dogfood runs after AUG-059 closed.\nEvidence: docs/dogfood/2026-10-27-domain-coverage-integration.md (legs M/G/C); raw logs ~/.hermes/stand-in/dogfood/auger/run18/logs/{legB,legC,legD}.log and the raw-PATCH arms recorded there. Filed by tick auger-dogfood-2026-10-27-15-09-28.","acceptance_criteria":"1) Fixture: a scratch DuckBrain (throwaway data dir) on port 3918; export DUCKBRAIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3918 and DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY from the minted token; `python3 auger.py -n df18 init --seed-domains`; `python3 auger.py -n df18 start --name drill --seed-file seed.txt`. Expected outcome: for each of 4.01, 4.03, 4.09 and 4.44, after `python3 auger.py -n df18 answer --id D-0NN --chosen x --option x --option y --why-not y --domain 4.03`, `curl -H \"x-api-key: $DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY\" \"$DUCKBRAIN_URL/api/ns/df18/tables/domain?num