 {"id": "AUG-112", "title": "[P2] The coverage map is blind to evidence when the domain row is absent: on the gridless path the README blesses, `status` reports 'answered 0' and lists the covered domain as ABSENT while the decision table holds a decision carrying its number", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-10-27T15:32:37Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-27T21:09:46Z", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["domain-coverage", "status", "docs"], "reasoning": "README's Quick start and its 'grid not found' note tell a user they may run WITHOUT `init --seed-domains` ('the domain rows are the coverage map, not a prerequisite for the loop'), and `answer --domain 4.05` works on such a box because the grid DIRECTORY is readable even when no rows are seeded.\nArm (namespace df18g, scratch substrate :3918, HEAD a9c979bcd2ab6a92a5ef4f513b5b030e0a67169a): `init` (no --seed-domains) -> 14/14; `start --name gridless` -> seed stored; `answer --id D-001 ... --domain 4.05` -> rc=0, 'D-001 recorded (domain 4.05 = data, ...)'; `dump` prints '## D-001  (4.05)  conf 0.82'. Then `status` prints:\n  'domain grid coverage (44 in the grid | 0 seeded | 44 absent):' / '  answered 0 (a decision or question row carries the num) | NOT-REACHED 0 (no such row)' / '  ABSENT (...): 4.01, ..., 4.05, ...'.\nGround truth from the substrate in the same minute: GET /api/ns/df18g/tables/decision -> [{\"id\":\"D-001\",\"domain\":\"4.05\",\"status\":\"decided\"}]; GET .../tables/domain -> 0 rows. So the report is right about the ROWS and wrong about the COVERAGE: the user's real question ('which domains have I answered?') gets 0 while an answer for 4.05 is stored.\nThe code contradicts itself here: `domain_coverage`'s own docstring (auger.py:4000-4020) says \"'answered' is EVIDENCE, not a status word \u2014 a domain is answered when a decision or a question row carries its number, so the report never depends on a status write nobody performed\", but the filter at auger.py:4053-4056 additionally requires `ln[\"row\"] is not None and not ln[\"off_grid\"]`, so a num that carries evidence with no `domain` row is counted nowhere \u2014 not in `answered`, not in `not_reached` (which is `seeded - answered` and is 0 here), and its evidence count is never printed.\nEvidence: docs/dogfood/2026-10-27-domain-coverage-integration.md (leg G); raw log ~/.hermes/stand-in/dogfood/auger/run18/logs/legB.log (ARM G block) and ~/.hermes/stand-in/dogfood/auger/run18/logs/g3_status.out. Filed by tick auger-dogfood-2026-10-27-15-09-28.", "acceptance_criteria": "Fixture: a scratch DuckBrain with a throwaway data dir; export DUCKBRAIN_URL to that instance's port (for example http://127.0.0.1:3918); `python3 auger.py -n df18g init` (WITHOUT --seed-domains); `python3 auger.py -n df18g start --name gridless --seed-file seed.txt`; `python3 auger.py -n df18g answer --id D-001 --chosen \"one SQLite file per box\" --option \"one SQLite file per box\" --option \"a shared Postgres\" --why-not \"Postgres needs a service\" --domain 4.05`.\n1) Expected outcome: `python3 auger.py -n df18g status` does not print 'answered 0' while the decision table holds a row with domain 4.05 \u2014 assert `auger status | grep -c 'answered 0'` is 0, and confirm the stored row with `curl -H \"x-api-key: $DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY\" \"$DUCKBRAIN_URL/api/ns/df18g/tables/decision?select=id,domain\"`.\n2) Expected outcome: the coverage block names 4.05 as carrying evidence with no `domain` row (one line naming both), so nothing the user has decided disappears from the report; probe `auger status -n df18g | grep -E '4\\.05'` prints a line mentioning the evidence count.\n3) Expected outcome: `auger status` and `auger dump` agree about 4.05 \u2014 dump prints '(4.05)' for D-001 today; after the fix the coverage block must not contradict it. Probe: both commands on the same namespace, both outputs in the verification artifact.", "depends_on": [], "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": "Worker produced 