 {"id":"AUG-113","title":"[P3] skills/auger-usage/SKILL.md coaches three behaviours that no longer exist on HEAD: `--domain` is validated now, the coverage display is not one-index-off, and the '(row status NOT-REACHED)' suffix is a failed write rather than a display quirk","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"status":"complete","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T18:07:53Z","created_by":null,"capability_tags":["docs","skill","coverage-guard"],"reasoning":"The usage skill is the surface a later agent ACTS on, so stale coaching costs real work and masks regressions. Re-run against HEAD a9c979bcd2ab6a92a5ef4f513b5b030e0a67169a (~/.hermes/stand-in/dogfood/auger/run18/logs/legB.log, legC.log):\n  (a) '`--domain` is unvalidated free text (AUG-038)' and 'Still live: `answer --domain` accepts any string (4.99, and even `notanumber`, both recorded exit 0)'. MEASURED NOW: `--domain 4.99` rc=1, `--domain notanumber` rc=1, `--domain data` rc=1, `--domain 4.9` rc=1, `--domain 4.05=data` rc=1 — each 'refused: unknown domain ... --domain takes one of the canonical grid numbers 4.01-4.44 (44 domains); nothing was stored'. AUG-038 is complete (commit 5422123).\n  (b) 'status's domain-coverage display is one-index-off — do not copy a domain number from status; look it up in the grid dir'. MEASURED NOW: the 44 (num, name) pairs status prints are exactly the 44 grid file names ('4.05  data' <-> 4.05-data.md); a copy-from-status lookup is correct. (My first census reported a diff — that was my parser reading the separate 'coverage by domain' summary block, not the product.)\n  (c) '`status`'s domain lines can contradict themselves (AUG-059) ... trust the leading word and the decisions/questions count, not the parenthetical.' The parenthetical is NOT display noise: it means the advance write failed (see AUG-059-R2, filed this tick), so 'trust the leading word' hides a real broken write on 35 of 44 domains.\nThis run corrected (a)-(c) in place in skills/auger-usage/SKILL.md (the sentence that misleads, edited — no 'UPDATE:' appended underneath), and the row exists so the prose cannot drift again silently: the guard below is what keeps a doc's claims in step with the rows they cite.\nEvidence: docs/dogfood/2026-10-27-domain-coverage-integration.md; ~/.hermes/stand-in/dogfood/auger/run18/logs/{legB,legC}.log; the committed skill diff. Filed by tick auger-dogfood-2026-10-27-15-09-28.","acceptance_criteria":"1) skills/auger-usage/SKILL.md no longer claims the domain flag is unvalidated: `grep -c 'unvalidated free text' skills/auger-usage/SKILL.md` returns 0, and the same section states the accepted form (the grid number, 4.01-4.44) with AUG-038 cited as closed. Expected outcome: both greps behave as stated on the committed blob.\n2) Every arm the old text recorded as exit 0 now refuses non-zero on HEAD: `auger answer --id T-1 --chosen x --option x --option y --why-not y --domain notanumber` rc=1; the same with `--domain 4.99` rc=1; `--domain data` rc=1; `--domain 4.9` rc=1. Expected outcome: 4/4 non-zero and nothing stored (read the decision table back after each).\n3) The AUG-059 caveat states the real mechanism and cites AUG-059-R2: `grep -c 'AUG-059-R2' skills/auger-usage/SKILL.md` is >= 1, and the sentence no longer tells the reader to distrust the parenthetical without saying what it means. Expected outcome: the file's coverage caveat names the failed row advance.\n4) A committed repo test drives the doc's own claim so the drift cannot recur silently: a test that runs the domain flag with an unknown value against a scratch namespace and asserts a non-zero exit plus 'nothing was stored', and a test that asserts the (num, name) pairs from `auger status` equal the grid directory's file names. Expected outcome: both pass on HEAD, and editing the doc to the old false claim makes the first test fail.","depends_on":[],"files_changed":["skills/auger-usage/SKILL.md","tests/test_auger.py","tests/test_usage_skill.py"],"foreman_note":"Wave