 {"id":"AUG-117","title":"[P1] pytest teardown orphans DuckBrain registry mappings: DELETE 409/429 still lets rmtree run, so the namespace directory vanishes while the mapping survives","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"status":"complete","created_at":"2026-10-28T03:49:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T05:40:15Z","created_by":null,"capability_tags":[],"reasoning":"tests/conftest.py documents teardown as 'down both paths' \u2014 DELETE /api/namespaces/<ns> plus shutil.rmtree of ~/duckbrain/namespaces/<ns>. When DELETE returns 409 'Push in flight' (documented in tests/PERF.md) or 429, rmtree still executes, so the directory disappears while the registry mapping does not: a permanent ghost row. Measured 2026-10-27 on the live substrate: 15,932 auger-pytest mappings existed in duckbrain.config.json, 15,268 of them with no directory, alongside 677 leaked directories (1.10 GB) and 176 stale .s3state manifests; auger's own leak audit only ever checked what it could see from the API/disk pair, so it read this as a concurrent session's in-flight namespaces rather than a leak. Result: 98.4% of DuckBrain's namespace listing was auger test garbage (2 MB payload for 276 real namespaces).","acceptance_criteria":"1. Teardown ordering is ownership-correct: the DELETE path owns removal (it clears the registry mapping AND the directory). If DELETE fails for any reason other than 404/absent-directory, teardown MUST NOT rmtree that directory \u2014 it leaves mapping+directory consistent and raises the failure, so nothing is ever orphaned into mapping-without-dir.\n2. The 429 path keeps its documented single-retry semantics, and the retry MUST clear the mapping before the 'skip with note' exit; a namespace left listed by GET /api/namespaces after retries is reported as a teardown problem, never a silent skip.\n3. Post-teardown verification asserts absence in the REGISTRY, not just on disk: the name must not appear in GET /api/namespaces.\n4. Regression test A: monkeypatched transport returns 409 'Push in flight' for DELETE \u2192 teardown leaves BOTH mapping and directory present, raises, and writes nothing destructive.\n5. Regression test B: transport returns 429 then success \u2192 after the retry the name is absent from GET /api/namespaces AND from disk (no mapping-only or dir-only residue).\n6. Suite-level leak audit asserts zero 'auger-pytest-<session-tag>-*' rows in GET /api/namespaces at session end (registry check, not disk-only), so a future ordering regression fails CI instead of accumulating silently.","depends_on":[],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"tick=auger-foreman-2026-10-28-04-31-58 block=AUG-117 wave=.coding-hermes/waves/auger-foreman-2026-10-28-04-31-58.json commit=6fe905f","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"6fe905f","completed_at":null,"guard_result":"SKIP","ci_result":"GREEN","detail":{"fingerprint":"ba88dcfa1d1d979b33bc529e388f303836e33afe5072c2f697b1d33bf44864fa","evidence":[{"run_id":"auger-foreman-2026-10-28-04-31-58","ts":"2026-10-28T05:40:15Z"}]},"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"worker_summary":"AUG-117 landed: teardown is BOTH-or-NEITHER \u2014 a settled DELETE (2xx/404) removes the directory; a refused DELETE (409/429/5xx) keeps it and reports the problem. Includes 3 regression tests. Gate: syntax+lint PASS, offline pytest 354 passed/6 failed (all 6 proven pre-existing baseline on origin/main 30f4f65 \u2014 422 proposed_by_model), hosted CI green."}
 {"id": "GATE-RED-002", "title": "[P1] main's live-arm gate is RED (6 tests): propagate/ask PATCH 'question' returns 422 \u2014 Column 'proposed_by_model' (varchar) requires a string, got null", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-10-28T05:41:06Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-28T05:41:06Z", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["python", "substrate-contract", "testing"], "reasoning": "Found 2026-10-28 by tick auger-foreman-2026-10-28-04-31-58 while verifying AUG-117. `bash tests/gate.sh` on the merged tree is RED at the pytest arm on exactly 6 tests, all in the ask/propagate path, each dying at auger.py:817 `patch()`: SystemExit: patch question failed (422): {'error': \"Column 'proposed_by_model' (varchar) requires a string, got null in table 'question'\", 'code': 'UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY'} from propagate() -> patch(ns, 'question', pk='Q-000002', values={'jev_already_answered': 0.93, 'jev_checked_at': '...'}). PROVEN PRE-EXISTING and not a diff artifact: the identical 6 tests fail identically on a CLEAN origin/main worktree (30f4f65, no changes) with the same 422 in 16.91s. Failing tests: test_ask_generated_paraphrase_is_rejected_using_bounded_stored_question_context, test_propagate_links_a_question_the_gate_can_answer_after_its_parent_closes, test_the_gate_links_an_answer_held_in_a_sibling_namespace, test_the_gate_survives_a_sibling_namespace_that_cannot_answer, test_a_namespace_declared_before_the_cross_project_edge_columns_keeps_working, test_the_gate_with_no_bundle_membership_recalls_its_own_namespace_only. Impact: the repo's own guard (gitreins test_command = bash tests/gate.sh, test_mode full) is RED on every CODE commit, so any real change must either fix this or be committed with --no-verify \u2014 a standing bypass, which is the real cost. Hosted CI stays GREEN because it runs AUGER_CI=1 and SKIPS the live arms, so CI does NOT see this. Direction (auger-side vs substrate-side) is unproven as of filing: either auger's PATCH