ASS (pytest 6 passed on merged tree)", "ci_result": "green (CI runs all success)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "13acb2b974f90f805ee98f084db865a22c48316ca451258ed4d087844bfa96d9"}, "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocked_since": null, "worker_summary": "Worker fixed the substrate null-refusal bug: added patch_or_rewrite() that falls back to DELETE+INSERT when a PATCH hits 'got null' on stored null columns. Changed set_state() and propagate() to use patch_or_rewrite instead of patch, removing the blank-proposal workaround. Also removed redundant concurrent.futures ThreadPoolExecutor from cmd_ask. Added two new tests. All 6 gate tests now PASS.", "dispatched_at": "2026-10-29T00:05:00Z", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/auger-GATE-RED-002", "branch": "wt/GATE-RED-002", "primary_model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "primary_provider": "deepseek-foreman"}
 {"id":"QA-AUGER-15","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"title":"[P2] clean-machine QA battery is invalidated by bunker-mvp ENOSPC before ci-pass/upgrade can run","reasoning":"QA tick auger-qa-2026-10-29-16-54-28 launched the full bunker battery against HEAD 2fcff58447c8ae8be16227587fad2c1c95387b13 on fresh agent 58b58514 @ bunker-mvp. The agent-side qa-run.log records mkdir failure for qa-act-wf because there was no space left on device, a failed ci.yml link, and another ENOSPC while creating the errorpath fixture. The evidence then reports ci-pass FAIL native rc=120 with no command output, upgrade FAIL rc=120 with no pip output, chaos-disconnect UNVERIFIED because ci-pass failed first, and chaos-resource UNVERIFIED because its 3 GiB cap was not applied and the suite ran uncapped. The server was already at 95% disk / 142.4 GB of 149.9 GB before launch and showed 59 containers; this is a bunker capacity/harness finding, not an auger product failure. Fresh install itself succeeded (auger-0.3 + pyyaml-6.0.3), and chaos-errorpath reached a clean rc=1 before the later ENOSPC path. This supersedes no existing open root-cause row: QA-AUGER-13 concerns substrate lock/session-state collapse, while this run's first failure is host disk exhaustion.","acceptance_criteria":"PASS: before a full battery is admitted, bunker-mvp has sufficient free disk for the agent and its CI workspace, or the launcher routes to a server with adequate headroom. PASS: re-run the full bunker battery for auger at the same or a later HEAD with no ENOSPC in qa-run.log or per-cell logs; ci-pass and upgrade must produce real command output, and chaos-resource must record cap applied in child/subshell/parent. PASS: a low-disk server is refused or clearly classified as harness UNVERIFIED without emitting product FAIL cells. PASS: the exact server disk reading, agent id, evidence path, and first ENOSPC lines remain attached to the QA record.","depends_on":[],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note